---
/**
 * Analytics consent notice.
 *
 * Google Analytics sets cookies, so it is not loaded at all until someone says
 * yes. The banner is hidden by default and only revealed when no choice is
 * stored yet: an inline script in BaseLayout adds `consent-pending` to <html>
 * before paint, and global.css keys off that class, so there is no flash.
 */
---

<div
  class="consent-banner fixed bottom-4 left-4 z-40 max-w-[calc(100vw-2rem)] rounded-lg border border-terracotta/30 bg-paper/95 p-4 shadow-lg backdrop-blur sm:max-w-md"
  role="region"
  aria-label="Analytics consent"
>
  <p class="text-sm text-ink">
    I use Google Analytics to see which posts get read. It sets cookies.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted">
    Saying no changes nothing about how the site works.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
    <button
      type="button"
      data-consent-accept
      class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-md bg-terracotta px-3 font-sans text-sm font-medium text-paper transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
    >
      Allow analytics
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      data-consent-decline
      class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-md border border-ink/50 px-3 font-sans text-sm text-ink transition-colors hover:border-terracotta hover:text-terracotta"
    >
      No thanks
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
